   "filas": [
    {
     "Final addressee": "Adif",
     "Number": "54/13-1",
     "Recommendation": "Make it a rule that all speed reductions, from a certain deceleration onwards, must be marked on the track by fixed speed limit signs."
    },
    {
     "Final addressee": "Adif",
     "Number": "54/13-2",
     "Recommendation": "For these situations (significant speed reductions), arrange progressive set-up of balises which may help to control the speed of trains, so that they brake in case the speed limit for entry into the next section is lowered. Therefore, implement the necessary ASFA Digital (Automatic Braking and Announcement of Signals) systems."
    },
    {
     "Final addressee": "Renfe Operadora",
     "Number": "54/13-3.1",
     "Recommendation": "Reinforce the procedures set in the Renfe Operadora SMS so that safety-related defects detected at any level are referred to the departments with the prescribed function of analysing and considering them, thereby assuring effective preventive management."
    },
    {
     "Final addressee": "DGF",
     "Number": "54/13-3.2",
     "Recommendation": "The national railway safety authority will ensure that Recommendation 54/13-3.1 is extended to the other railway undertakings."
    },
    {
     "Final addressee": "DGF",
     "Number": "54/13-4",
     "Recommendation": "The national railway safety authority should consider whether to reconvene the Joint Traffic Safety Committees, including representatives from Adif and the railway undertakings, and under the authority’s supervision. These committees can analyse risk situations deriving from the interaction between driving, vehicle and track."
    }
   ],
   "cita": "| Final addressee | Number | Recommendation |"
  },
  {
   "pagina": 110,
   "cabecera": [
    "DGF",
    "54/13-5",
    "The process of commissioning new railway lines and alternative stretches should include a specific risk assessment. This should include identification and management of possible hazards driving from the interaction between subsystems, in normal and degraded operating conditions, and their links with the driving and traffic staff involved when a train is travelling from beginning to end of the line or alternative stretch, and its connection to the existing network. Also analyse the viability of the layout at the various construction stages. In justified cases, promote the application of such assessments to lines which are in service."
   ],
   "filas": [
    {
     "DGF": "DGF",
     "54/13-5": "54/13-6",
     "The process of commissioning new railway lines and alternative stretches should include a specific risk assessment. This should include identification and management of possible hazards driving from the interaction between subsystems, in normal and degraded operating conditions, and their links with the driving and traffic staff involved when a train is travelling from beginning to end of the line or alternative stretch, and its connection to the existing network. Also analyse the viability of the layout at the various construction stages. In justified cases, promote the application of such assessments to lines which are in service.": "Make the necessary arrangements for communications with driving staff in the cab to take place safely and avoid possible distractions. Make these arrangements part of the general regulations and pass them on to the railway undertakings for inclusion in their safety management systems."
    },
    {
     "DGF": "Renfe Operadora",
     "54/13-5": "54/13-7.1",
     "The process of commissioning new railway lines and alternative stretches should include a specific risk assessment. This should include identification and management of possible hazards driving from the interaction between subsystems, in normal and degraded operating conditions, and their links with the driving and traffic staff involved when a train is travelling from beginning to end of the line or alternative stretch, and its connection to the existing network. Also analyse the viability of the layout at the various construction stages. In justified cases, promote the application of such assessments to lines which are in service.": "Promote the progressive implementation of an audio recording system in drivers’ cabs. Assess the feasibility of adding a video recording system as well."
    },
    {
     "DGF": "DGF",
     "54/13-5": "54/13-7.2",
     "The process of commissioning new railway lines and alternative stretches should include a specific risk assessment. This should include identification and management of possible hazards driving from the interaction between subsystems, in normal and degraded operating conditions, and their links with the driving and traffic staff involved when a train is travelling from beginning to end of the line or alternative stretch, and its connection to the existing network. Also analyse the viability of the layout at the various construction stages. In justified cases, promote the application of such assessments to lines which are in service.": "The national railway safety authority will ensure that Recommendation 54/13-7.1 is extended to the other railway undertakings."
    }
   ],
